\description{
Retrieve Financial Statement Data for Listed Securities Companies (HK)
}
\details{
The length of \code{stock_codes} must be between 1 and 100. When assigning
a value to \code{start_date}, the length of \code{stock_codes} must be 1. Either
\code{start_date} or \code{date} must be provided. Passing \code{latest} as the value for
\code{date} will retrieve the most recent financial statement data within the
last 1.1 years. \code{limit} is only effective when requesting data within a date
range. When the length of \code{stock_codes} is greater than 1, a maximum of 48
metrics can be selected; when the length of \code{stock_codes} equals 1,
a maximum of 128 metrics can be retrieved.

Metrics are specified using the format:
\verb{[granularity].[tableName].[fieldName].[expressionCalculateType]}.

Supported granularities:
\itemize{
\item \code{y}: Annual
\item \code{hy}: Half-year
\item \code{q}: Quarterly
}

Supported expression calculation types for quarterly data:
\itemize{
\item \code{t}: Current period
\item \code{t_o}: Current period original value
\item \code{t_y2y}: Current period year-over-year
\item \code{t_c2c}: Current period quarter-over-quarter
\item \code{c}: Single quarter
\item \code{c_o}: Single quarter original value
\item \code{c_y2y}: Single quarter year-over-year
\item \code{c_c2c}: Single quarter quarter-over-quarter
\item \code{ttm}: Trailing twelve months
\item \code{ttm_o}: TTM original value
\item \code{ttm_y2y}: TTM year-over-year
\item \code{ttm_c2c}: TTM quarter-over-quarter
}

Table names and field names for securities companies include:
\itemize{
\item \code{ps}: Profit Statement (e.g., \code{ps.oi} for operating income)
\item \code{bs}: Balance Sheet
\item \code{cf}: Cash Flow Statement
}

Example: \code{"q.ps.oi.t"} retrieves quarterly operating income (current period cumulative).
}
